# Dev checks (enforced, not advisory)

A check that only lives in a doc gets skipped — by people, by v0, by Lovable, by agents. Every gate below is wired to something that fails the push or the deploy.

## The scripts

| Script | Runs | When |
|---|---|---|
| `typecheck` | type check, no emit | standalone — hosts look for this exact name |
| `lint` / `lint:fix` | linter | standalone |
| `check` | `check:entry-files` → `lint:fix` → `lint` → `typecheck` | before every push |
| `pipeline` / `predeploy` | `check` + test + build + e2e (see `predeploy.mdc`) | before merge to `main`, Next.js / full-gate stacks |

TanStack Start / builder-first repos have no `predeploy`: ship gate is `check` + `build`.

## Three enforcement layers

| Layer | Mechanism | Catches |
|---|---|---|
| Local | `.githooks/pre-push` runs `check`; `core.hooksPath` set by `setup` (`scripts/setup-git-hooks.mjs`, also on `postinstall`) | lint/type errors before they cost a CI or deploy run |
| CI | `.github/workflows/ci.yml` — install `--frozen-lockfile` → typecheck → lint → build on every PR and push to `main` | anything the hook skipped (`--no-verify`, web-editor commits, AI-builder commits) |
| Host | Vercel Checks (`lint` + `typecheck` scripts) — see `docs/environment/vercel.md` | deploy-time gate; a missing script is *skipped*, not passed |

Hook + CI + host all call the **same script names** — never inline a different command in one layer.

## Iteration vs. push

- While iterating on UI: don't run the gates after every edit — `dev` only.
- Run `check` before push, `/review` and `/push`-style skills; run `pipeline` before merge.
- Stage any `lint:fix` diffs — never push with lint failures.
- Never bypass with `--no-verify`, `continue-on-error`, `// @ts-ignore`/`eslint-disable` to get green. Fix or ask.
- Never lower a threshold (bundle size, coverage, lint severity) without explicit user OK.

## Hook rules

- Hooks live in `.githooks/` (committed), never `.git/hooks/`.
- Hook exits 0 immediately when `CI`, `GITHUB_ACTIONS`, or `VERCEL` is set.
- Hook stays fast: `check` only. Build/e2e belong to `pipeline` and CI.
- `setup-git-hooks.mjs` is a no-op without `.git` (tarball installs, Vercel) and never fails install.
